name conllu
# CoNLL-U. A sentence is a record: its notes, then a row for every word. The columns are named as Universal
# Dependencies' format names them; every value is recorded as the treebank writes it. What the treebank says of the
# words, column by column, is a layer down the sentence; of each word, the value it gives it. How it numbers its
# sentences, documents and paragraphs (sent_id, newdoc id, newpar id) is how it points at them: recorded nowhere.
match *.conllu
grammar table
columns ID FORM LEMMA UPOS XPOS FEATS HEAD DEPREL DEPS MISC
comment #
record blank
empty _
note =
about text
key sent_id "newdoc id" "newpar id" newdoc newpar
word FORM
number ID -
attest LEMMA UPOS XPOS
pairs FEATS | = ,
pairs MISC | =
relation DEPREL to HEAD
relations DEPS | :
